---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../site.js';
const schema = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebSite', name: SITE_NAME, url: 'https://loadplancalc.com/' };
---
<Base title={SITE_NAME} description="Free load planning calculators: see how many cartons fit in a shipping container, with a 3D loading plan, plus container dimensions from carriers' published specifications." schema={schema}>
  <section class="prose">
    <h1>Plan your container load before the truck arrives</h1>
    <p class="lede">Free calculators that show how many cartons fit in a container, how much space and payload you use, and a 3D plan you can step through and share. Nothing to install, no sign-up.</p>
    <div class="card-list">
      <a class="card" href="/container-loading-calculator/"><strong>Container loading calculator</strong><span>Mixed carton sizes into a 20', 40', 40' HC or 45' container, with a 3D plan.</span></a>
      <a class="card" href="/pallet-loading-calculator/"><strong>Pallet loading calculator</strong><span>How many cartons fit on a Euro, EPAL or 48 × 40 in pallet: Ti-Hi, height and weight limits, 3D plan.</span></a>
      <a class="card" href="/how-many-pallets-fit-in-a-container/"><strong>How many pallets fit in a container</strong><span>Euro, EPAL and 48 × 40 in pallets in a 20', 40', 40' HC or 45', one or two high, with a 3D plan.</span></a>
      <a class="card" href="/how-many-pallets-fit-in-a-53-foot-trailer/"><strong>How many pallets fit in a 53 ft trailer</strong><span>48 × 40 in, Euro and EPAL pallets in a 53' dry van, one or two high, with a 3D plan.</span></a>
      <a class="card" href="/cbm-calculator/"><strong>CBM calculator</strong><span>Cartons to cubic meters and cubic feet, and the share of each container's volume.</span></a>
      <a class="card" href="/cubic-feet-calculator/"><strong>Cubic feet calculator</strong><span>Length × width × height in inches, feet, cm or m to cubic feet, cubic meters and cubic yards, plus a ft³ ⇄ m³ converter.</span></a>
      <a class="card" href="/dimensional-weight-calculator/"><strong>Dimensional weight calculator</strong><span>Box size and weight to dimensional and billable weight: the USPS rule (139) or your carrier's divisor.</span></a>
      <a class="card" href="/shipping-container-dimensions/"><strong>Shipping container dimensions</strong><span>Inside sizes, doors, volume and payloads from Hapag-Lloyd's specifications.</span></a>
      <a class="card" href="/53-foot-trailer-dimensions/"><strong>53 ft trailer dimensions</strong><span>Inside length, width and height of 53' dry vans and reefers in ft-in and mm, from the makers' spec sheets.</span></a>
      <a class="card" href="/pallet-sizes/"><strong>Standard pallet sizes</strong><span>Euro pallet, EPAL 2, 3, 6, 7 and the 48 × 40 in pallet: size, height, weight and load.</span></a>
      <a class="card" href="/how-to-use/"><strong>How to use the planner</strong><span>Step-by-step guide: boxes, orientation, loading steps, editing the 3D plan by hand, sharing.</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose">
    <h2>What makes a plan trustworthy</h2>
    <p>Every plan is checked before it is shown: no overlapping boxes, every box supported, “this side up” respected, door size and weight limit enforced. Container sizes link to the carrier's own specification page. <a href="/how-we-calculate/">How we calculate</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
